Error [E0068]: This callable uses the retired result-arrow shape.
  --> tests/ui/E-CALL-VALUE_call_result_not_called.jet:1:28
    |
  1 | fn make_adder() => fn(Int) => Int :: (value: Int) => value + 1
    |                            ^^
 Why: a return type sits after the parameter list, and `->` introduces the body; an effect ceiling follows the return type
 Fix: write `fn name(...) Type -> body`, or `fn name(...) Type -[Effects]> { … }`

Error [E0068]: This callable uses the retired result-arrow shape.
  --> tests/ui/E-CALL-VALUE_call_result_not_called.jet:1:17
    |
  1 | fn make_adder() => fn(Int) => Int :: (value: Int) => value + 1
    |                 ^^
 Why: a return type sits after the parameter list, and `->` introduces the body; an effect ceiling follows the return type
 Fix: write `fn name(...) Type -> body`, or `fn name(...) Type -[Effects]> { … }`

Error [E0065]: This function uses the retired `::` body marker.
  --> tests/ui/E-CALL-VALUE_call_result_not_called.jet:1:35
    |
  1 | fn make_adder() => fn(Int) => Int :: (value: Int) => value + 1
    |                                   ^^
 Why: A one-expression function body uses `->`; `::` binds a name, and `=` fills a slot inside a definition.
 Fix: Replace `::` with `->`; `jet fmt` applies this fix.

Error [E0070]: this uses a retired arrow spelling
  --> tests/ui/E-CALL-VALUE_call_result_not_called.jet:1:51
    |
  1 | fn make_adder() => fn(Int) => Int :: (value: Int) => value + 1
    |                                                   ^^
 Why: callables, arms, and lambdas use one arrow: `->`
 Fix: replace `:>` or `=>` with `->`

Error [E-CALL-VALUE]: a function value is invoked with the retired adjacent-call spelling
  --> tests/ui/E-CALL-VALUE_call_result_not_called.jet:4:23
    |
  4 |     print(make_adder()(1))
    |                       ^
 Why: named functions and direct field, index, or lambda calls keep their spelling; a returned call result uses `.call(…)` so the value and invocation stay explicit (D-CALLVALUE1=B)
 Fix: write `callee.call(…)`
